\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 4.1 Introduction to projects.locations.config.get (SDK: client.get_config)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
Given that model availability, language support, and features evolve rapidly\'97as evidenced by the GA announcement for Chirp 2 in 2025 in specific regions 
\fs32 \cf3 \cb5 \super \strokec3 6
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \nosupersub \strokec2 \'97relying solely on static documentation is insufficient. The definitive, runtime method for programmatically determining regional capabilities is the \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 projects.locations.config.get\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  API.
\fs32 \cf3 \cb5 \super \strokec3 3
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \nosupersub \strokec2 \
This API provides location metadata detailing the languages, models, and model features available within a specific region.
\fs32 \cf3 \cb5 \super \strokec3 16
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \nosupersub \strokec2  The REST endpoint for this resource follows the format: \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 projects/\{project\}/locations/\{location\}/config\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 .
\fs32 \cf3 \cb5 \super \strokec3 17
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \nosupersub \strokec2  In the Python SDK, this is exposed via the \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 client.get_config()\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  method.
\fs32 \cf3 \cb5 \super \strokec3 13
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \nosupersub \strokec2 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 4.2 Python Implementation for Programmatic Regional Query\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
Successful querying of regional capabilities requires adherence to the V2 architectural principle of regional client binding. The client used to query the configuration must be initialized to the regional endpoint matching the configuration resource name.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
