\f1\b\fs36 \cf2 V. Implementation Guide: Deploying Regional Recognizers in Python\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
This section provides the necessary Python steps to correctly configure the client and resource path, thereby resolving the $400$ routing error for \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 batch_recognize\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  using the Chirp model.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 5.1 Correct SpeechClient Initialization for Regional Access\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
The use of \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 ClientOptions\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  to override the default global endpoint is the essential first step for any regional V2 operation, especially when using Chirp.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb7 \strokec3 Python\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf3 \
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf9 \cb7 \strokec9 import\cf3 \strokec3  os\
\cf9 \strokec9 from\cf3 \strokec3  google.api_core.client_options \cf9 \strokec9 import\cf3 \strokec3  ClientOptions\
\cf9 \strokec9 from\cf3 \strokec3  google.cloud.speech_v2 \cf9 \strokec9 import\cf3 \strokec3  SpeechClient\
\cf9 \strokec9 from\cf3 \strokec3  google.cloud.speech_v2.types \cf9 \strokec9 import\cf3 \strokec3  cloud_speech \
\
PROJECT_ID = os.getenv(\cf10 \strokec10 "GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT"\cf3 \strokec3 , \cf10 \strokec10 "your-project-id"\cf3 \strokec3 )\
REGION = \cf10 \strokec10 "us-central1"\cf3 \strokec3  \cf13 \strokec13 # Must be a region where Chirp is supported, e.g., us-central1 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf13 \strokec13 # 1. Instantiate the client pointing to the specific regional endpoint.\cf3 \strokec3 \
\cf13 \strokec13 # This ensures that all subsequent requests are routed through the regional service boundary.\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf9 \strokec9 try\cf3 \strokec3 :\
    client = SpeechClient(\
        client_options=ClientOptions(\
            api_endpoint=\cf10 \strokec10 f"\cf2 \strokec2 \{REGION\}\cf10 \strokec10 -speech.googleapis.com"\cf3 \strokec3 , \
        )\
    )\
    print(\cf10 \strokec10 f"SpeechClient initialized for regional endpoint: \cf2 \strokec2 \{REGION\}\cf10 \strokec10 -speech.googleapis.com"\cf3 \strokec3 )\
\cf9 \strokec9 except\cf3 \strokec3  Exception \cf9 \strokec9 as\cf3 \strokec3  e:\
    print(\cf10 \strokec10 f"Client Initialization Error: \cf2 \strokec2 \{e\}\cf10 \strokec10 "\cf3 \strokec3 )\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 The region in the client endpoint 
\f1\b must match
\f0\b0  the location in the Recognizer path. If the endpoint is configured regionally (e.g., \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 us-central1\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ), the request will be successfully routed, and the service will then expect a \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 recognizer\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  path containing \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 locations/us-central1\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 .\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 5.2 Creating an Explicit Regional Recognizer for Chirp\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
While implicit recognizers (\cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 recognizers/_\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ) can be used, defining an explicit, named Recognizer is recommended for production environments as it simplifies configuration reuse and tracking.
\fs32 \cf3 \cb5 \super \strokec3 9
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \nosupersub \strokec2  The parent path for creation must contain the target region.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb7 \strokec3 Python\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf3 \
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf9 \cb7 \strokec9 def\cf3 \strokec3  \cf11 \strokec11 create_regional_chirp_recognizer\cf3 \strokec3 (client: SpeechClient, project_id: \cf12 \strokec12 str\cf3 \strokec3 , region: \cf12 \strokec12 str\cf3 \strokec3 , recognizer_id: \cf12 \strokec12 str\cf3 \strokec3 ):\
    \cf10 \strokec10 """Creates a Recognizer resource scoped to the specified region."""\cf3 \strokec3 \
    \
    parent_path = \cf10 \strokec10 f"projects/\cf2 \strokec2 \{project_id\}\cf10 \strokec10 /locations/\cf2 \strokec2 \{region\}\cf10 \strokec10 "\cf3 \strokec3 \
    \
    \cf13 \strokec13 # Define the configuration using the regional Chirp model\cf3 \strokec3 \
    config = cloud_speech.RecognitionConfig(\
        auto_decoding_config=cloud_speech.AutoDetectDecodingConfig(),\
        language_codes=,\
        model=\cf10 \strokec10 "chirp"\cf3 \strokec3 , \cf13 \strokec13 # Use the regionally supported model\cf3 \strokec3 \
    )\
    \
    request = cloud_speech.CreateRecognizerRequest(\
        parent=parent_path, \
        recognizer_id=recognizer_id,\
        recognizer=cloud_speech.Recognizer(\
            display_name=\cf10 \strokec10 f"Chirp Recognizer in \cf2 \strokec2 \{region\}\cf10 \strokec10 "\cf3 \strokec3 ,\
            default_recognition_config=config,\
        ),\
    )\
    \
    \cf13 \strokec13 # The client (initialized regionally in 5.1) sends the request to the regional service.\cf3 \strokec3 \
    operation = client.create_recognizer(request=request)\
    recognizer = operation.result()\
    print(\cf10 \strokec10 f"Created Regional Recognizer: \cf2 \strokec2 \{recognizer.name\}\cf10 \strokec10 "\cf3 \strokec3 )\
    \cf9 \strokec9 return\cf3 \strokec3  recognizer.name\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
