\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 5.3 Executing BatchRecognize with Regional Resource References\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
The final \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 BatchRecognize\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  request uses the fully qualified regional name of the Recognizer. Because the client was initialized with the matching regional endpoint (Section 5.1), the request is successfully routed and validated by the regional service boundary, resolving the initial $400$ error.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb7 \strokec3 Python\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf3 \
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf9 \cb7 \strokec9 def\cf3 \strokec3  \cf11 \strokec11 run_regional_batch_recognize\cf3 \strokec3 (client: SpeechClient, recognizer_name: \cf12 \strokec12 str\cf3 \strokec3 , gcs_uri: \cf12 \strokec12 str\cf3 \strokec3 ):\
    \cf10 \strokec10 """Runs a batch recognition request using a specific regional recognizer."""\cf3 \strokec3 \
    \
    request = cloud_speech.BatchRecognizeRequest(\
        recognizer=recognizer_name,\
        files=,\
    )\
    \
    print(\cf10 \strokec10 f"Starting Batch Recognize using regional recognizer: \cf2 \strokec2 \{recognizer_name\}\cf10 \strokec10 "\cf3 \strokec3 )\
    \
    \cf13 \strokec13 # The regionally-bound client executes the request.\cf3 \strokec3 \
    operation = client.batch_recognize(request=request) \
    \
    print(\cf10 \strokec10 "Waiting for batch operation to complete..."\cf3 \strokec3 )\
    result = operation.result()\
    print(\cf10 \strokec10 "Batch operation completed."\cf3 \strokec3 )\
    \cf9 \strokec9 return\cf3 \strokec3  result\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

